{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>For</b> — The punishment and the evil that comes upon a person is called עון, for it was the cause of the evil's coming, as in: גדול עוני (Lamentations 1:8), ויגדל עון בת עמי (Lamentations 4:6), אם יקרך עון (Job 36:23). And likewise: the expression ולא יכלתי לראות על דרך וכסה את עין הארץ, because my iniquities are without number; or: and I could not see the appearance of the heart, as in: וירא יעקב (Genesis 31:1)." "<b>And my heart has forsaken me</b> — As if I remained without a heart."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:25.719263229Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}